  "preamble": "In Estonian and Votic, and more rarely Livonian, Proto-Finnic short *o unrounded to the close-mid back unrounded vowel õ [ɤ] in a number of words: *kova 'hard' > Estonian and Votic kõva, *korva 'ear' > Estonian kõrv. Finnish keeps o (kova, korva). The change is distinct from the southern Finnic development of õ from *e (*ë) in back-vowel words.",
